---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import Byline from "../../components/Byline.astro";
import DualDoors from "../../components/DualDoors.astro";
import CompanyMint from "../../components/CompanyMint.astro";
import { BRIEFS } from "../../lib/briefs";
import { LINKS, linkClass, ext } from "../../lib/links";
import { newsArticleNode } from "../../lib/schema";
import { withBase } from "../../lib/base";

const brief = BRIEFS.find((b) => b.slug === "nics-is-not-consumer-demand")!;

const crumbs = [
  { name: "Home", path: "/" },
  { name: "Notes", path: "/brief" },
  { name: brief.title, path: brief.path },
];

const pageUrl = "https://fflintel.com/brief/nics-is-not-consumer-demand";
const hero = brief.image;
const sourceUrl =
  "https://www.theoutdoorwire.com/releases/2026/09/nssf-adjusted-nics-background-checks-for-august-2026/";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`${brief.title} | FFL Intel`}
  description={brief.dek}
  path={brief.path}
  ogImagePath={hero}
  breadcrumbs={crumbs}
  showDoors={false}
  extraJsonLd={[
    newsArticleNode({
      url: pageUrl,
      headline: brief.title,
      description: brief.dek,
      datePublished: brief.date,
      dateModified: brief.date,
      image: `https://fflintel.com/${hero}`,
    }),
  ]}
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-12 sm:py-14">
    <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
    <p
      class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-sky-800 mb-3"
    >
      {brief.kicker}
    </p>
    <h1
      class="font-serif text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl text-balance mb-4"
    >
      {brief.title}
    </h1>
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-stone-700 mb-6">{brief.dek}</p>
    <Byline dateLabel={brief.dateLabel} read={brief.read} />

    <figure class="mt-8 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-stone-200">
      <img
        src={withBase(hero)}
        alt={brief.imageAlt}
        width="1280"
        height="720"
        class="w-full object-cover max-h-80"
      />
      <figcaption class="px-4 py-2 text-[11px] text-stone-500">
        An empty indoor range lane.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div
      class="mt-8 space-y-5 text-[1.05rem] leading-[1.7] text-stone-700 font-serif"
    >
      <p>
        NSSF published its August 2026 adjusted NICS figure this week (<a
          href={sourceUrl}
          class={linkClass}
          {...ext}>Outdoor Wire, September 2026</a
        >). The adjusted count is 1,115,410, up 2.2 percent from 1,091,342 in
        August 2025. The unadjusted FBI NICS print for August 2026 is
        1,917,379, up 10.0 percent from 1,743,509 a year earlier.
      </p>
      <p>
        Those two lines already disagree with each other. That is the first
        warning. The second is what NSSF itself subtracts, and what it refuses
        to claim.
      </p>
      <p>
        NSSF builds the adjusted series by removing purpose-code permit checks
        and permit rechecks. States use those codes for CCW applications and
        for sweeps of active permit databases. They are not a sale at the
        counter. Starting in February 2016, NSSF also subtracts permit
        rechecks. That cleanup is real. It still leaves a check count, not a
        sales count.
      </p>
      <p>
        Twenty-eight states run at least one qualified alternative permit under
        the Brady Act. A permit holder who already cleared a background check
        to get that permit can buy from a licensed dealer without a separate
        NICS check on that transfer. Those legal transfers never appear as NICS
        checks. NSSF does not adjust for them. In those states, the print
        understates how many guns moved.
      </p>
      <p>
        New for 2026, NSSF is also publishing monthly NFA Form 1 and Form 4
        checks. August printed 185,744, up 201.6 percent from 61,594 in August
        2025. Texas led the month at 28,030, then Florida, Georgia, North
        Carolina, and Pennsylvania. That is market insight on NFA paperwork. It
        is still not retail sales demand. It does not say which models sold, at
        what price, or whether a shopper who typed a name ever found one.
      </p>
      <p>
        NSSF’s own line is the one to keep. The adjusted series is not a
        direct correlation to firearms sales. The statistics are checks
        initiated. They are not guns sold. They are not sales dollars. State
        law, local conditions, and purchase scenarios break any one-to-one
        link between a background check and a firearm sale. Used guns, multiple
        guns on one check, denials, and the twenty-eight-state permit path are
        why a rising Monday print can still leave a manufacturer guessing what
        to build and a retailer guessing what to put on the wall.
      </p>
      <p>
        A better NICS series still cannot see the search that never rang.
        Someone opened a dealer site, typed a model, and got nothing back.
        Empty never becomes a check. Empty never becomes a unit. It is still
        demand.
      </p>
      <p>
        We will not invent a search-intent print to set beside 1,115,410. If a
        Betsy line belongs next to this Note, that is a verified ask later.
        Sell-through and search are different jobs. Keep the series apart.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10">
      <p
        class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-sky-800 mb-3"
      >
        Three numbers. Keep them apart.
      </p>
      <div
        class="overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-rule bg-white shadow-sm"
      >
        <table class="w-full min-w-[28rem] text-left text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="border-b border-rule bg-stone-50">
              <th
                class="px-3 py-3 text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-sky-800"
              >
                Number
              </th>
              <th
                class="px-3 py-3 text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-stone-500"
              >
                What it is
              </th>
              <th
                class="px-3 py-3 text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-stone-400"
              >
                What it is not
              </th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="border-b border-rule/80 align-top">
              <td class="px-3 py-3 text-xs font-medium text-ink">
                NICS (FBI or NSSF-adjusted)
              </td>
              <td class="px-3 py-3 text-xs text-stone-700 leading-relaxed">
                Firearm background checks initiated
              </td>
              <td class="px-3 py-3 text-xs text-stone-500 leading-relaxed">
                Guns sold, or sales dollars
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-rule/80 align-top">
              <td class="px-3 py-3 text-xs font-medium text-ink">
                Sell-through
              </td>
              <td class="px-3 py-3 text-xs text-stone-700 leading-relaxed">
                New guns that left the same stores as last year
              </td>
              <td class="px-3 py-3 text-xs text-stone-500 leading-relaxed">
                What people searched for
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="align-top">
              <td class="px-3 py-3 text-xs font-medium text-ink">
                Search intent
              </td>
              <td class="px-3 py-3 text-xs text-stone-700 leading-relaxed">
                What people typed, including empty results
              </td>
              <td class="px-3 py-3 text-xs text-stone-500 leading-relaxed">
                A sales report
              </td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div
      class="mt-8 space-y-5 text-[1.05rem] leading-[1.7] text-stone-700 font-serif"
    >
      <p>
        If you make the guns →{" "}
        <a href={LINKS.demandIntel} class={linkClass} {...ext}
          >Demand Intelligence</a
        >
      </p>
      <p>
        If you sell them →{" "}
        <a href={LINKS.gsa} class={linkClass} {...ext}>GunSearchAgent</a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <DualDoors />
    <CompanyMint />

    <div
      class="mt-8 space-y-5 text-[1.05rem] leading-[1.7] text-stone-700 font-serif"
    >
      <p>
        <a href="https://fflintel.com" class={linkClass}>FFL Intel</a> is the
        journal of these three numbers.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-10 text-xs leading-relaxed text-stone-500">
      NSSF-Adjusted NICS Background Checks for August 2026,{" "}
      <a href={sourceUrl} class={linkClass} {...ext}>The Outdoor Wire</a>.
      Marks of their owners. Not affiliated with NSSF. Published by Coriolis,
      LLC. Numbers by Betsy.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
